Tau Ceti f790474821cf4256814db967cb154e7af3d0c369. NOT COMPILED.

Two layers. The first is executable against the pinned Mathlib polynomial API:
the q-integer as a geometric sum, the Jackson q-difference operator on the
polynomial ring in one variable, the twisted Leibniz rule, the vanishing of the
square of the induced differential in one variable, and the specialisation at
q = 1. The second layer is signatures only. Neither pinned library has filtered
or graded objects in an enhanced derived category, animation, the decalage
functor, prismatic cohomology, Lambda-rings, delta-rings, q-Witt vectors or
Habiro completion, so every object above the elementary layer appears as a
`variable` or as a declaration with a placeholder proof.

Conventions fixed here and used throughout, matching the roadmap document:

* `[n]_q` is the geometric sum of the first `n` powers of `q`; the q-de Rham
  prism ideal is generated by `[p]_q`, NOT by `q - 1`.
* A filtered object is descending, constant in degrees at most zero, and the
  filtered ring is `(q-1)^* A[q]`, presented as `A[β,t]/(β*t - (q-1))` with
  `β` in degree 1 and `t` in degree -1.
* `fil^* M / (q^m - 1)` ALWAYS means the base change with `q^m - 1` in
  filtration degree ONE, not the degreewise quotient.
* No `Prop` standing for "is a q-Hodge filtration" is introduced as an opaque
  hypothesis, and no axiom is used. Where a contract cannot yet be stated, the
  declaration is a signature and the document carries the statement.
-/
